{
  "scope": "Native classic checkpoint transport. Every measured candidate board, used mask, stack, scalar, ownership field and dtype was compared with a fresh full snapshot. No change to the search order.",
  "hardware": "RTX 2060, 6 GB",
  "timing": "Source, driver warmup and other experiments varied. These comparisons measure work and bytes. Dedicated codec timings are separate.",
  "board_recovery": "Physical deltas, all 9/16-bit modes, every raw inventory bit, corrupt CPU frame/depth inputs, sparse/dense directories, 65536 boundary, 131072 lanes, invalid packet fallback and immutable generations were checked against independent native readback.",
  "decision": "Reuse an independent device mirror when available. Price actual changes, compact the directory on device, retain exact changed-cell masks to avoid a second full scan of dirty lanes. Stateless physical fallback reads original board cells and the five actual inventory words.",
  "rejected": "Native frame reconstruction could disagree with physical cells for stale host depths or cursors. Independent mirrored reconstruction required more host uploads, and CPU-planned deltas repeated lane/extent transfers.",
